Little XM Tracker on Mortar. Every change is behind MORTAR_BUILD (set by
pkgs/little-xm-tracker); other builds are unchanged.

- TrackerApp.cpp, controller(): the app names buttons after the Brick's
  printed labels and upstream relies on KNULLI's patched SDL mapping for
  that. Here SDL auto-maps the evdev pad (A = BTN_EAST = SDL "B", B =
  BTN_SOUTH = SDL "A"), so swap them, and in the --ui-test fixture too.
- BitmapFont.cpp: ASCII text from a glyph atlas instead of one fill rect per
  pixel. A pattern screen took about 100 ms a frame on the A53s that way, a
  whole core at 10 fps, playing or not. Same pixels; Unifont glyphs unchanged.
- TrackerApp.cpp, run(): the whole screen is redrawn every frame. With no
  input for 500 ms, nothing playing and no worker busy, redraw at 4 fps; while
  the shell has the focus (the app is hidden), at 1 fps, playing or not.
  Events are still polled and the audio thread is unaffected.
- TrackerSession.inc: theme presets and the mapping file are copied from the
  read-only store and would stay read-only; upstream means them to be edited.

